According to TS 24.301, clause 4.4.4.3 ("Integrity checking of NAS signalling messages in the UE"):

> "the UE shall accept the following NAS signalling messages without integrity protection, even though the specific NAS signalling procedure requires that the message shall be integrity protected:
> - ATTACH REJECT;
> - IDENTITY REQUEST (if requested identification parameter is IMSI);
> - AUTHENTICATION REQUEST;
> - AUTHENTICATION REJECT;
> - DETACH ACCEPT (for non‑EPS services);
> - DETACH REQUEST (for non‑EPS services);
> - TRACKING AREA UPDATE REJECT; and
> - EMM STATUS (if sent in response to any of the above messages)."
